# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A tilde suppresses the link families TiddlyWiki suppresses"

# TiddlyWiki reads a leading tilde as a suppressor for three link families: wikilinkprefix
# hands back plain text for a CamelCase word, and extlink and syslink each return the text
# of the link they declined to make. A pretty link takes no suppressor — the parser builds
# the link and leaves the tilde standing as content.

! A CamelCase word links, and a suppressed one does not

A CamelCaseLink and a ~CamelCaseSuppressed here.
# ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.link.wikilink.tiddlywiki5
#                      ^ - meta.link.wikilink.tiddlywiki5
#                      ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.link.suppressed.wikilink.tiddlywiki5

! An external link, suppressed

See https://example.com/a and ~https://example.com/b here.
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5
#                              ^ - markup.underline.link.external.tiddlywiki5
#                              ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.link.suppressed.external.tiddlywiki5

! A system link, suppressed

See $:/a/link and ~$:/b/link here.
#   ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.underline.link.syslink.tiddlywiki5
#                  ^ - markup.underline.link.syslink.tiddlywiki5
#                  ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 meta.link.suppressed.syslink.tiddlywiki5

! A pretty link takes no suppressor, and keeps its own reading

A ~[[Pretty Link]] stands linked.
#  ^ text.html.tiddlywiki5 meta.paragraph.tiddlywiki5 markup.link.tiddlywiki5 punctuation.definition.link.outer.begin.tiddlywiki5

